NNAAMMEE
       dbus-update-activation-environment - update environment used for D-Bus
       session services

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ddbbuuss--uuppddaattee--aaccttiivvaattiioonn--eennvviirroonnmmeenntt [--systemd] [--verbose] --all |
                                          _V_A_R... | _V_A_R=_V_A_L...

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ddbbuuss--uuppddaattee--aaccttiivvaattiioonn--eennvviirroonnmmeenntt updates the list of environment
       variables used by ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn ----sseessssiioonn when it activates session
       services without using ssyysstteemmdd.

       With the ----ssyysstteemmdd option, if an instance of ssyysstteemmdd ----uusseerr is
       available on D-Bus, it also updates the list of environment variables
       used by ssyysstteemmdd ----uusseerr when it activates user services, including D-Bus
       session services for which ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn has been configured to delegate
       activation to ssyysstteemmdd. This is very similar to the iimmppoorrtt--eennvviirroonnmmeenntt
       command provided by ssyysstteemmccttll(1)).

       Variables that are special to ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn or ssyysstteemmdd may be set, but
       their values will be overridden when a service is started. For
       instance, it is not useful to add DDBBUUSS__SSEESSSSIIOONN__BBUUSS__AADDDDRREESSSS to
       ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn's activation environment, although it might still be useful
       to add it to ssyysstteemmdd's activation environment.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       ----aallll
           Set all environment variables present in the environment used by
           ddbbuuss--uuppddaattee--aaccttiivvaattiioonn--eennvviirroonnmmeenntt.

       ----ssyysstteemmdd
           Set environment variables for systemd user services as well as for
           traditional D-Bus session services.

       ----vveerrbboossee
           Output messages to standard error explaining what
           dbus-update-activation-environment is doing.

       _V_A_R
           If _V_A_R is present in the environment of
           ddbbuuss--uuppddaattee--aaccttiivvaattiioonn--eennvviirroonnmmeenntt, set it to the same value for
           D-Bus services. Its value must be UTF-8 (if not, it is skipped with
           a warning). If _V_A_R is not present in the environment, this argument
           is silently ignored.

       _V_A_R=_V_A_L
           Set _V_A_R to _V_A_L, which must be UTF-8.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
       ddbbuuss--uuppddaattee--aaccttiivvaattiioonn--eennvviirroonnmmeenntt is primarily designed to be used in
       Linux distributions' X11 session startup scripts, in conjunction with
       the "user bus" design.

       To propagate DDIISSPPLLAAYY and XXAAUUTTHHOORRIITTYY to ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn and, if present,
       ssyysstteemmdd, and propagate DDBBUUSS__SSEESSSSIIOONN__BBUUSS__AADDDDRREESSSS to ssyysstteemmdd:

                   dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd \
                       DBUS_SESSION_BUS_ADDRESS DISPLAY XAUTHORITY


       To propagate all environment variables except XXDDGG__SSEEAATT, XXDDGG__SSEESSSSIIOONN__IIDD
       and XXDDGG__VVTTNNRR to ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn (and, if present, ssyysstteemmdd) for
       compatibility with legacy X11 session startup scripts:

                   # in a subshell so the variables remain set in the
                   # parent script
                   (
                     unset XDG_SEAT
                     unset XDG_SESSION_ID
                     unset XDG_VTNR

                     dbus-update-activation-environment --systemd --all
                   )



EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
       ddbbuuss--uuppddaattee--aaccttiivvaattiioonn--eennvviirroonnmmeenntt exits with status 0 on success,
       EX_USAGE (64) on invalid command-line options, EX_OSERR (71) if unable
       to connect to the session bus, or EX_UNAVAILABLE (69) if unable to set
       the environment variables. Other nonzero exit codes might be added in
       future versions.

EENNVVIIRROONNMMEENNTT
       DDBBUUSS__SSEESSSSIIOONN__BBUUSS__AADDDDRREESSSS, XXDDGG__RRUUNNTTIIMMEE__DDIIRR and/or DDIISSPPLLAAYY are used to
       find the address of the session bus.

LLIIMMIITTAATTIIOONNSS
       ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn does not provide a way to unset environment variables after
       they have been set (although ssyysstteemmdd does), so
       ddbbuuss--uuppddaattee--aaccttiivvaattiioonn--eennvviirroonnmmeenntt does not offer this functionality
       either.

       POSIX does not specify the encoding of non-ASCII environment variable
       names or values and allows them to contain any non-zero byte, but
       neither ddbbuuss--ddaaeemmoonn nor ssyysstteemmdd supports environment variables with
       non-UTF-8 names or values. Accordingly,
       ddbbuuss--uuppddaattee--aaccttiivvaattiioonn--eennvviirroonnmmeenntt assumes that any name or value that
       appears to be valid UTF-8 is intended to be UTF-8, and ignores other
       names or values with a warning.

